{"title":"Ogre Warchief","html":"<article class=\"wp\"><div class=\"wp-main\"><p class=\"wp-lede\">A level 54 Ogre that attacks with crush (melee).</p>\n      <h2>Fighting it</h2><div class=\"s\"><i>Weak</i> <span class=\"tag-chip weak\">burn</span><span class=\"tag-chip weak\">freeze</span><span class=\"tag-chip weak\">shock</span><span class=\"tag-chip weak\">crush</span> &nbsp; <i>Resists</i> <span class=\"tag-chip resist\">stab</span></div>\n      <p class=\"s muted\">A weakness adds 30% damage and a resistance takes 30% off (the game's own rule).</p>\n      \n      \n      <p class=\"s\"><b>Reagent:</b> <a href=\"#/item/giants-knucklebone\">Giants Knucklebone</a> <span class=\"muted\">(infuses an enchant)</span>, <a href=\"#/item/ogre-bone-needle\">Ogre Bone Needle</a> <span class=\"muted\">(crafting catalyst)</span>. About 1 kill in 500, 1 in 50 from an elite. <a href=\"#/guide/reforging\">Enchanter’s Table</a></p>\n      <h2>Levels</h2><div class=\"q-picker\" role=\"group\" aria-label=\"Level\"><a class=\"q-chip\" href=\"#/monster/ogre-warchief\">All levels</a><a class=\"q-chip on\" href=\"#/monster/ogre-warchief?lv=54\">Lv 54 <span>56</span></a><a class=\"q-chip\" href=\"#/monster/ogre-warchief?lv=56\">Lv 56 <span>104</span></a><a class=\"q-chip\" href=\"#/monster/ogre-warchief?lv=59\">Lv 59 <span>96</span></a><a class=\"q-chip\" href=\"#/monster/ogre-warchief?lv=60\">Lv 60 <span>196</span></a><a class=\"q-chip\" href=\"#/monster/ogre-warchief?lv=61\">Lv 61 <span>165</span></a><a class=\"q-chip\" href=\"#/monster/ogre-warchief?lv=62\">Lv 62 <span>35</span></a></div>\n      <p class=\"s muted\">The same monster spawns at different levels, and its hitpoints, damage and XP follow its level (the game’s own formula). In the game a monster more than 5 levels above you shows its level as “???”.</p>\n      <div class=\"g-scroll\"><table class=\"g-table q-table\"><thead><tr><th>Level</th><th>HP</th><th>Damage</th><th>XP</th><th>Elite (HP · dmg · XP)</th><th>Seen</th>